{
  "repo": "ARMOR-NODE-HMI",
  "ecosystem": "armor",
  "tagline": "The touch panel of the house: it shows what the server knows, takes the PIN on the screen and talks to the assistant; it carries out no command by itself.",
  "description": "The firmware of ARMOR-NODE-HMI drives a 7-inch touch screen, a speaker and four microphones on a Waveshare ESP32-S3 board, shows the summary that ARMOR-SERVER sends, marks it stale when it is old and never shows the duress alarm. The firmware has been built once with ESP-IDF 5.5.5 and has never run on a board.",
  "columns": [
    "WHAT IS CONNECTED",
    "THIS FIRMWARE",
    "WHO IT TALKS TO"
  ],
